# Deliberate, justified Trivy exceptions. Each entry names a CVE that is
# present in an image but provably not reachable in Helio's usage, with the
# condition under which it should be re-evaluated. This is read automatically
# by the Trivy scan in .github/workflows/release.yml.

# CVE-2025-68121 — Go crypto/tls "incorrect certificate validation during TLS
# session resumption". Reaches Helio in two upstream binaries, neither of which
# exercises the affected path:
#   - backup image: the `gosu` v1.19 privilege-drop helper bundled by
#     postgres:16-alpine (su-exec symlinks to it). gosu opens no network/TLS
#     connections, so the crypto/tls code is dead in that binary.
#   - updater image: the Docker CLI's own Go stdlib (docker:28-cli). The updater
#     drives `docker compose` against the LOCAL daemon over a Unix socket (no
#     TLS); registry pulls run in the daemon, not the CLI, so the CLI's TLS
#     session-resumption path is not reached.
# No rebuilt upstream bases ship a fixed Go yet. Re-evaluate (and drop this line)
# once postgres:16-alpine's gosu and docker:28-cli are built with Go >= 1.24.13.
CVE-2025-68121

# CVE-2026-33186 — grpc-go authz "authorization bypass via improper HTTP/2 path
# validation". Carried by google.golang.org/grpc (v1.74.2) linked into the
# Docker CLI in the updater image (docker:28-cli). The flaw is in grpc-go's
# server-side authorization interceptor (google.golang.org/grpc/authz); the
# updater's Docker CLI acts only as a gRPC CLIENT to the local daemon/BuildKit
# over a Unix socket and runs no authz-protected gRPC server (and pulls rather
# than builds images), so the vulnerable interceptor is never invoked. Re-evaluate
# (and drop this line) once docker:28-cli ships grpc-go >= 1.79.3.
CVE-2026-33186

# CVE-2026-31789 — OpenSSL "heap buffer overflow on 32-bit systems from a large
# X.509 certificate". Carried by libcrypto3/libssl3 (3.5.4-r0) in the Docker
# CLI's Alpine base (docker:28-cli) in the updater image. The overflow is, per
# the advisory, specific to 32-bit builds; Helio's images are built and run on
# 64-bit targets (amd64 / arm64) only, where the affected path does not trigger.
# Re-evaluate (and drop this line) once docker:28-cli's Alpine base ships
# openssl >= 3.5.6-r0.
CVE-2026-31789
